{"title":"2018 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 Part B","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.5</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2\" title=\"2018 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A bag contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> balls numbered from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72287b09043ed45b372a517d764e12d07aff8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643ce6c9bcdd122a6cfb8e2492a1f5264e238549.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times (n - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" /> ways in which Julio can remove one ball from the bag and then remove a second ball. This is because there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> possible choices for the first ball and then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e80c6b6a84ad4015ea436a915435d69edbdd96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> possible choices for the second ball. For example, when a bag contains 6 balls numbered from 1 to 6, 4 of which are black and 2 of which are gold, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3baf0066ce7886d39f68ef8e6ac40747eaf9ca6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 5 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> ways in which he can remove two balls in this way, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/0/bd0f8037d7acb21e0c73e5ae336584073ac16b8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 3 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> ways in which both balls are black.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2_Part_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c166641181de220405d2ace87e63dec334b26ab8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, a second bag contains 6 black balls and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> gold balls; the balls are numbered from 1 to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c7ad225b9c56afb998f5c877032c1ad5ac76d47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />. Julio removes two balls as described above. The probability that both balls are black is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. Determine the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2_Part_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the bag has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> black balls and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c7ad225b9c56afb998f5c877032c1ad5ac76d47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> balls in total, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3baf0066ce7886d39f68ef8e6ac40747eaf9ca6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 5 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> ways to pick two black balls from the bag and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee95a2641a77d3017c293e588cbeab46a9a1663a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(g + 6)(g + 5) = g^{2} + 6g + 5g + 30 = g^{2} + 11g + 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"405\" height=\"21\" /> ways to pick two balls from the bag. \n</p><p>The probability that both balls are black is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, so the number of ways to pick two balls from the bag must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the number of ways to pick two black balls from the bag, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/f/6df4608b7b1772fa1085325a8edeea38ff881362.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 \\times 8 = 240$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />. We then see:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c13e53e6550ffc9a6237f809d2437de562e6501.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g^{2} + 11g + 30 = 240$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/c/98ccf9e72fd5f3999ab427486cd5e170074b34d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g^{2} + 11g - 210 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d3e3dce1f4dcee557dc70166b40549b2ab32eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g^{2} + 21g - 10g - 210 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"201\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cdda46cc21d7fc14f6123a483cf8b94d4908a2c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(g + 21) - 10(g + 21) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"213\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/7/0374c476e4ae2168695536305b8fef10d9cd66c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(g - 10)(g + 21) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This means that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc65c2a3bde54b44358f55a0a1358c76390df003.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/5/4750049767b3b654db85a2ac42fb7959771468c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g = -21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> represents a positive number, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b22e700787185e5051d8bbb813d7ac935b1f67d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{g = 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5\">Solution 1.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2_Part_B&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in solution 1, we can get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c13e53e6550ffc9a6237f809d2437de562e6501.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g^{2} + 11g + 30 = 240$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This means:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d658bfadee3d6af589c5ba8e4e086da98d6879d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(g + 11) = 240 - 30 = 210$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"218\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is positive and the divisors must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> apart, one of them must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the other must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b22e700787185e5051d8bbb813d7ac935b1f67d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{g = 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018062000\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 166/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 842/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6709/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   10.941      1 2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2\n100.00%   10.941      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37105:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018062000 and revision id 286431. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}